# The macOS dylibs, pinned. fetch-dylibs.sh verifies each downloaded asset
# against this and refuses anything else, so this file -- not the rolling
# `latest` tag -- is what makes the fetch reproducible.
#
# Neither dylib is committed. Git keeps every version of a tracked file for
# ever, so a binary on main charges every clone of this repository -- and of
# anything using it as a submodule -- for versions nobody will run again,
# including the clones that will never touch macOS. Release assets are not
# reachable from any ref, so a clone pays nothing and only the machines
# assembling a macOS bundle download them.
#
# Bumping either one is two steps and the second is not optional: upload the new
# dylib to the release, then commit the new hash here. Until that commit lands
# every fetch fails on the mismatch, which is the intended failure -- the
# alternative is shipping a binary nobody chose.
#
#   libvulkan_kosmickrisp.dylib   Mesa's Vulkan-on-Metal driver, built by
#                                 vendor-kosmickrisp.sh, which prints the
#                                 upload command. 15 MB, bumped with Mesa.
#   libvulkan.1.dylib             the Khronos loader, built by
#                                 vendor-vulkan.yml. 1.4 MB, changes about
#                                 once a year.
#
# Columns: sha256, file name, and the version the bytes were built from -- the
# version is what makes a bad bump recoverable, since the way back is to
# rebuild that exact version.
c98d6fffd38478ece406fb6bb359aedf4b4a8efe86f1345e963a5a9c23393ad5  libvulkan_kosmickrisp.dylib  mesa-26.3.0-devel
092cdfd0699a1556c747ce6120b17202e02a7ba9406ba3b11ebd8029e285da44  libvulkan.1.dylib            vulkan-sdk-1.4.350.1
